🕵️‍♂️ Rogue-Investigator: The Pythonic ECS Template

This project serves as a "Gold Master" template for grid-based Roguelikes. It is built using Python 3.10+, tcod, and tcod-ecs. It emphasizes a clean separation of concerns and a data-driven architecture.


🛠 Project Architecture

This template follows the Entity Component System (ECS) paradigm, favoring Composition over Inheritance.

    main.py: The entry point. Initializes the root console and manages the core game loop.

    game/states.py: The "Brain" of the operation. Handles input logic, collision detection, and state transitions using a State Machine pattern.

    game/world_tools.py: The "Map Bureau." Contains logic for procedural generation, boundary math, and entity spawning.

    game/components.py: The "Data Schema." Defines what an entity is and has (Position, Graphic, Gold, etc.).

    game/state_tools.py: Visual utilities, including the "Screen Dimmer" for menu transitions.

🚀 Key Features

    Collision Physics: Entities with the "Solid" tag act as physical barriers.

    Dynamic Inventory: Automatic gold pickup and real-time total tracking.

    Debug Overlay: Mouse-over coordinate tracking (printed to console) for forensic spatial testing.

    Scalable Map Logic: Easy-to-adjust x_min/max variables for custom room sizes.

🚦 How to Use

    Clone the Template: Use this folder as the root for any new Roguelike.

    Define Components: Add new data types in components.py.

    Expand the World: Modify world_tools.py to create new room shapes or dungeon floors.

    Add Mechanics: Nest new interaction logic inside the on_event match statements in states.py.